CHAPTER.VERS:
Why have we fasted, [they say], and you don't see? [Why] have we afflicted our soul, and you take no knowledge? Look, in the day of your

          {+}
         fast you

          {+}
         find [your

          {+}
         own] pleasure, and exact all your

          {+}
         labors.

Look, you

          {+}
         fast for strife and contention, and to strike with the fist of wickedness: you

          {+}
         do not fast this day so as to make your

          {+}
         voice to be heard on high.

Isn't this the fast that I have chosen: to loose the bonds of wickedness, to undo the bands of the yoke, and to let the oppressed go free, and that you

          {+}
         break every yoke?
